iran is accusing israel and promising  revenge for the ambush shooting death of  a top scientist who has been described  as a key figure behind iran's nuclear  bomb program  almost two decades ago the attack  happened on friday in a suburb of tehran  the capital  roxanna saberi is in our london bureau  with the latest roxanna good morning  good morning dana iran's supreme leader  ali hominy is calling for the assassins  to be  punished iran's president is also  promising revenge while blaming  israel for the attack the comments come  a day after mossein factory zade was  killed in broad daylight while traveling  near tehran  iran's defense minister said the car  carrying the scientists was shot at  before a truck bomb exploded nearby iran  says factory zadeh was a college  professor but the u.s and israel have  alleged he led a secret nuclear arms  program  and in 2018 prime minister benjamin  netanyahu singled out factory zadah in a  news conference  accusing him of conducting nuclear  weapons work under the guise of a  civilian program  israel has not yet commented on  yesterday's attack but iran has accused  it of killing other nuclear scientists  in the past decade  whoever killed factory zonda his death  is likely to raise tensions  between washington and tehran earlier  this month president trump reportedly  asked senior advisors  about options to attack iran's main  nuclear site but was dissuaded  neither the white house nor the biden  transition team has commented yet on  yesterday's killing but president-elect  biden has suggested  he'll rejoin an international nuclear  deal that president trump left  in 2018. ed roxanna thanks
 

